# Changed by Sanctuary Computer (quickbooks-mcp-286, quickbooks-mcp-293, quickbooks-mcp-294): the five keys the read server reads, and below them the four more the write server needs and the two it passes on to the receipt command (all commented out).
# Every value below is a placeholder. Copy this file, set real values in your own environment, and never commit them.
# The server holds no QuickBooks refresh token, client id or client secret: Stacks supplies an access token per company, which the server keeps in memory until 5 minutes before it expires.

# Required. The Stacks origin: https, no username, password, path, query or fragment.
STACKS_QBO_URL=https://stacks.example

# Required. The key the server sends to Stacks in the X-Api-Key header.
STACKS_QBO_TOKEN=replace-me

# Required. The path of the entities file (v 1.0) that lists the companies this server may use.
QBO_COMPANIES=/path/to/entities.json

# Required. Must be exactly: production
QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT=production

# Optional. Unset or read is the read server; write is the write server (see Write mode below); anything else, empty included, refuses. Leave it out unless you need it.
# QBO_MODE=read

# Write mode. Leave all of this out for the read server, which ignores it. For the write server, set QBO_MODE=write
# instead of the QBO_MODE=read line above, and set the four QBO_WRITE_ keys below: it refuses to start when one is not set or is empty.
# QBO_MODE=write

# Write mode, required. The receipt command.
# QBO_WRITE_RECEIPT_CMD=/path/to/receipt-command

# Write mode, required. The path of the off switch's file.
# QBO_WRITE_SWITCH=/path/to/write-switch

# Write mode, required. The path of writes.jsonl.
# QBO_WRITE_LEDGER=/path/to/writes.jsonl

# Write mode, required. The path of the job sweep's stamp.
# QBO_WRITE_SWEEP_STAMP=/path/to/sweep-stamp

# Write mode, optional. Passed to the receipt command, which is run with exactly NOTION_API_KEY, QBO_WRITE_LEDGER, PATH and TZ in its environment (each of NOTION_API_KEY, PATH and TZ only when set in the server's own environment). NOTION_API_KEY is the key the command writes the Notion Audit Log with.
# NOTION_API_KEY=replace-me

# Write mode, optional. Passed to the receipt command: the time zone the command runs in. PATH is passed the same way, from the server's own environment, and has no line here.
# TZ=America/New_York
